cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this work, please cite the methods note below.
type: article
title: "Configuration-Stable PairHMM Score Reduction"
abstract: >
  Measured configuration stability of a GATK-style PairHMM aggregate
  haplotype-score reduction under a canonical compensated policy.
  Unordered parallel reduction changed the haplotype-score fingerprint
  with thread count or GPU block size. The canonical policy did not,
  on the recorded workloads. This repository publishes the methods note
  and a closed Linux evaluation binary. It does not publish source code
  and does not license the LuxiEdge engine.
